            <ArticleTitle>[Therapeutic considerations on a case of post-transfusion intravascular hemolysis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>389-92</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case is presented of intravascular hemolysis following incompatible transfusion of 500 ml hetero-group blood in a patient aged 29 years that had undergone emergency surgery for intra-abdominal hemorrhagic syndrome. Stress is laid on volemic therapy, on osmotic treatment and on the administration of alkalines in the first hours following the accident.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
